    "> what do you recommend for sec-4?",
    "\n\nThe simplest and most effective fix: **minimum staking duration before revenue eligibility**.\n\n### Why this over alternatives\n\n| Approach | Complexity | Gas Cost | Effectiveness |\n|----------|-----------|----------|--------------|\n| **Min duration check** | Low — 1 new variable, 1 check in modifier | Zero extra gas on claims | ✅ Blocks flash stakes completely |\n| Epoch-based distribution | High — new epoch logic, claim windows, bookkeeping | Higher gas per distribution | Overkill for this use case |\n| Time-weighted shares (ve-style) | Very high — integral math, checkpoints | Significant gas overhead | Best fairness but complex |\n| Snapshot at distribution time | Medium — requires off-chain keeper to snapshot | Extra infra needed | Doesn't work fully on-chain |\n\n### Recommendation: Min duration check\n\nAdd a `minStakeDuration` (e.g., 24-48 hours). When the `updateRevenue` modifier runs, it only accrues revenue for users whose oldest active stake is older than `minStakeDuration`. This means:\n\n- Attacker stakes and immediately triggers revenue → gets nothing (stake too fresh)\n- Honest staker who's been in for days → gets their share normally\n- Zero extra gas on `notifyRewardAmount` or `claimRevenue`\n- Admin-configurable — can adjust the window\n\nThe check goes in the `updateRevenue` modifier — if the user hasn't been staking long enough, they simply don't accrue revenue from that distribution. Their `userRewardPerTokenPaid` still gets updated so they don't retroactively earn past distributions later.\n\nWant me to implement it?\n[Tool uses: none]",
    "> how does attacker stakes immidiately triigers revenue? show me such case",
    "\n\nThe attack works because `notifyRewardAmount` is permissioned — only `DISTRIBUTOR_ROLE` can call it. So the attacker can't directly trigger it. But here's the realistic scenario:\n\n### How it actually works\n\nThe attacker doesn't trigger the revenue themselves. They **front-run** a known revenue distribution transaction.\n\n```\nMempool shows: Marketplace.payRent(listingId) from tenant\n                → this will call staking.notifyRewardAmount(450 tokens)\n\nBlock N:\n  TX 1: Attacker stakes 900,000 tokens (front-runs with higher gas)\n  TX 2: Tenant's payRent() executes → 450 tokens distributed to pool\n  TX 3: Attacker claims revenue → gets 90% of 450 = 405 tokens\n  TX 4: Attacker unstakes via emergencyWithdraw() → gets 900,000 back\n```\n\nThe attacker's cost is just gas fees. They borrow 900k tokens (flash loan or own capital), hold them for 1 block, and extract 405 tokens of rental income that should have gone to honest long-term stakers.\n\n### Let me show you this in the test that already passed:\n[Tool uses: fs_read]",
