    "> oh its mev?",
    "\n\nYes, exactly. It's a form of MEV (Maximal Extractable Value). Specifically a **sandwich-style MEV attack** on the staking pool:\n\n```\n1. Attacker sees payRent() in mempool\n2. Front-run: stake huge amount (higher gas priority)\n3. Victim tx: payRent() → revenue distributed → attacker gets lion's share\n4. Back-run: emergencyWithdraw() + claimRevenue()\n```\n\nOn BSC this is especially easy because:\n- Validators can reorder transactions within a block\n- Mempool is public\n- Block time is ~3 seconds — plenty of time to react\n- No flashbots-style private mempool protection like Ethereum\n\nThe irony is your `HybridProxyAdmin` already protects against MEV on **upgrades** (immutable `_proxyAdmin` in constructor). This is the same class of problem but on the **staking revenue** side.\n\nThe min duration fix effectively makes the front-run useless — even if the attacker gets their stake in before the revenue tx, they won't be eligible to earn from it. Want me to implement it?\n[Tool uses: none]",
